From b57f02fcdf8258a72964a43be0ed3ca645e59ec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:30:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): each profile recovers only its own background
 jobs; finished jobs leave every checkpoint [daveey]

The multiplexed gateway's one ProcessRegistry wrote every live job into every profile's
processes.json, and a finished job left only the file of the profile that saw its exit. Each later
restart re-attached the finished job from another profile's stale copy (proc_05186a9e0419: alpha-follow
18:12Z, bb-tuner 19:11Z, ci-sweeper 20:12Z on 10-30) and wrote another result there.

- a job keyed agent:<profile>:... is written to and recovered from only that profile's checkpoint
  (agent:main = default only in a multiplexed registry); a non-owner hands its copy to the owner
- a job whose result receipt exists in any profile is never re-attached, and is dropped from every
  profile's processes.json when it finishes (one file lock at a time)
- multiplexed startup first settles finished copies and re-homes the rest (the one-time cleanup)

Tests: stale copy + foreign job (RED on main), startup cleanup, single-profile agent:main keys, and
a re-attached sandbox completion starting a turn in a live Slack session through the real
completion path (RED with the injection disabled).
